Te Urewera is an area of mostly forested, sparsely populated rugged hill country in the North Island of New Zealand, a large part of which is within a protected area designated in 2014, that was formerly Te Urewera National Park. Te Urewera is the rohe of Tūhoe, a Māori iwi known for its stance on Māori sovereignty.
[[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Te_Urewera|Wikipedia]]

