---
Hokitika is a town in the West Coast region of New Zealand's South Island, 40 kilometres south of Greymouth, and close to the mouth of the Hokitika River. It is the seat and largest town in the Westland District. The town's estimated population is 3,120 as of June 2023. On a clear day Aoraki / Mount Cook can clearly be seen from Hokitika's main street.
[[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hokitika|Wikipedia]]
