Whangamomona is a small township in the Stratford District and Manawatū-Whanganui Region in New Zealand. It lies on State Highway 43, the &quot;Forgotten World Highway&quot;, 65 kilometres north-east of Stratford and 55 kilometres south-west of Ohura. By rail it is 61 kilometres from Stratford on the Stratford-Okahukura railway line.
