    <cmt/>
    <desc>Présence du plus grand totara (Pouakani totara)
---
Pureora Forest Park is a 760-square-kilometre protected area in the North Island of New Zealand. Within its rich rainforest are an abundance of 1,000-year-old podocarp trees. It is &quot;recognised as one of the finest rain forests in the world&quot;. Established in 1978, after a series of protests and tree sittings, the park is one of the largest intact tracts of native forest in the North Island and has high conservation value due to the variety of plant life and animal habitats. New Zealand's largest totara tree is located nearby on private land.
[[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pureora_Forest_Park|Wikipedia]]

